      "narrative": "Mara Venn sets down her copper mug, the dull clink echoing through the near-empty tavern. Her sharp eyes hold yours as she leans forward, elbows on the scarred table.\n\n\"The Ash Gate's been sealed since Old Bram died. Three weeks ago now.\" She pauses, letting the fact settle. \"Bram was the ferryman \u2014 the only one who knew how to navigate the Grey Hind through the mists beyond that arch. When they found him dead at the landing, the gate masters ordered it shut. No boat, no passage.\"\n\nShe glances toward Toran Vex, who's hunched over a ledger at the next table, ink-stained fingers fidgeting with a quill.\n\n\"Toran there held the lock-warden's post for the Kestrel Guild. He knows the mechanism better than anyone. But even he can't open it without the ferryman's key \u2014 and that went missing the night Bram died.\"\n\nShe watches you, waiting to see if you'll press further or turn to the clerk."
    },
