      "narrative": "Mara Venn tilts her head, a flicker of curiosity crossing her face at your question.\n\n\"Filed? The lock isn't filed, friend. It's intact \u2014 just sealed.\" She gestures with a thumb toward the nervous clerk. \"Toran Vex maintained it for years. Sworn to the Kestrel Guild, lock-warden of the Ash Gate. He's the one who fitted the last mechanism Bram signed off on.\"\n\nShe lets that hang, then adds, \"If anyone knows the guts of that lock, it's him. Whether he'll talk about it is another matter.\"\n\nToran's quill scratches a nervous flourish across his ledger as he pretends not to listen. His ink-stained cuffs tremble slightly.\n\nMara watches you, waiting to see if you'll approach the clerk directly."
