      "narrative": "The question hangs in the air. Mara Venn's eyes narrow \u2014 not with hostility, but with the look of someone sifting through memory and coming up with dust.\n\n\"Old Bram sold passage,\" she says slowly. \"That was his charge. Ferryman takes the coin, opens the gate, rows you through the mist.\" She frowns, tapping a finger against her mug. \"But you're asking who else. Who authorized it. Who kept the books.\"\n\nShe shakes her head, frustration bleeding into her voice. \"I don't have a name for you. The Kestrel Guild's records would show it \u2014 manifests, toll ledgers, the whole mess. But those books...\" She trails off, jaw tightening. \"They're not here. They'd be in the guild archive, or maybe Bram kept copies at his quarters near the gate landing.\"\n\nShe meets your eyes, and there's an edge of apology in her voice. \"I can tell you how the system worked. I can't tell you who pulled the strings. I wasn't high enough in the guild to see those names.\"\n\nThe silence stretches. Across the room, Toran Vex's quill has gone still. He's no longer pretending not to listen."
    },
