      "narrative": "The name leaves your lips and falls into the stillness like a stone into deep water.\n\n\"Old Bram!\"\n\nThe mist does not stir. The rope does not move. No echo returns from the arch \u2014 the sound seems to soak into the grey curtain and vanish, swallowed whole.\n\nYou wait. Seconds stretch into half a minute. The only response is the faint, rhythmic hush of the mist churning against itself, a sound like distant breath.\n\nFrom somewhere behind you, further down the street, a crow calls once and falls silent.\n\nThe gate offers nothing. No footsteps. No voice. No sign that anyone has tended this landing in weeks."
